Workaround applied in pml-my only (NOT in pml-harmony): added a 4th sellable plan ("Ultra") to purchasable-plans.fixture.ts so the seeded catalog always has exactly 4 sellable plans, matching what PlanSelector's hardcoded default expects. The zero-price/non-sellable plan was kept as a 5th fixture entry to still exercise the "zero price plans are not shown" scenario.
Flagged as a real product/library bug candidate worth reporting upstream to whoever owns pml-harmony (still open/unfixed there): PlanSelector should either accept/derive numberOfCards dynamically from plans.length instead of relying on a caller-supplied prop that Catalog.tsx never actually passes, or react-slick's settings should not hardcode slidesToShow/initialSlide values disconnected from the actual slide count — production catalogs with fewer than 4 sellable plans (e.g. if plans are temporarily deactivated) would hit this exact same visual bug for real users, not just in tests.